1
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:47,750
[KING OF COMEDY]

2
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:50,870
[Episode 22]

3
00:02:27,590 --> 00:02:28,680
It's so cold out there.

4
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:29,680
Put the jacket on.

5
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:37,560
You put it on.

6
00:02:37,590 --> 00:02:38,560
No need. I can handle the cold.

7
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:39,400
-I'm wearing a lot of clothes.
-It's windy. Just put it on.

8
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,000
Don't catch a cold.

9
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,720
-I'm wearing a lot of clothes.
-You put it on.

10
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:43,780
You're indeed wearing more than I am.

11
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:46,760
Just going through the motions.

12
00:02:48,050 --> 00:02:49,730
Jiahao and I grew up together.

13
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,930
He is my most important family member.

14
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:57,310
But I didn't expect

15
00:02:57,310 --> 00:02:59,590
that protecting him in the way

16
00:02:59,990 --> 00:03:01,050
I thought was right

17
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:03,550
would actually hurt him.

18
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,240
As a sister,

19
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,640
am I doing a terrible job?

20
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:10,750
Actually...

21
00:03:10,950 --> 00:03:12,720
It doesn't seem that bad.

22
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:13,800
Right.

23
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:16,070
I just ignored his feelings a bit.

24
00:03:24,190 --> 00:03:25,590
Why don't you comfort me?

25
00:03:28,590 --> 00:03:30,590
I... I think you've figured it out.

26
00:03:30,590 --> 00:03:31,800
And what you said makes sense.

27
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:32,930
I've taken it all in.

28
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:35,190
Besides, I'm an only child.

29
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:36,920
So I don't have much say in this.

30
00:03:37,070 --> 00:03:39,000
I think what you said really makes sense.

31
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,400
Y-You're not taking me seriously!

32
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:41,800
You have to comfort me.

33
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:42,470
How do I comfort you?

34
00:03:42,470 --> 00:03:43,470
I'll comfort you.

35
00:03:43,540 --> 00:03:45,270
I'll comfort you. How do I do it?

36
00:03:45,310 --> 00:03:46,150
You won't comfort me, right?

37
00:03:46,150 --> 00:03:47,070
If you don't, give that knife...

38
00:03:47,070 --> 00:03:47,750
I will, I will.

39
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:49,190
-back to me.
-I'll comfort you.

40
00:03:49,190 --> 00:03:51,240
I... I'll tell you a story.

41
00:03:56,190 --> 00:03:57,000
Let me tell you

42
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,710
how I got started in show business.

43
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:00,400
Okay.

44
00:04:01,050 --> 00:04:02,030
They say

45
00:04:02,630 --> 00:04:04,290
a bad song beats a good speech.

46
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:05,940
I'll just perform it for you.

47
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:06,310
Okay.

48
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,760
Back then, because of this show,

49
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,910
directors faught to cast me.

50
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:12,470
Next show,

51
00:04:13,630 --> 00:04:15,360
the comedy sketch "Xiaozao".

52
00:04:15,590 --> 00:04:17,680
Performer: Zhenzhen's Ke.

53
00:04:18,430 --> 00:04:19,160
Ready.

54
00:04:19,490 --> 00:04:20,050
Action.

55
00:04:22,310 --> 00:04:23,360
What is this?

56
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:24,430
Everyone's gone.

57
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:26,400
The students have left.

58
00:04:27,190 --> 00:04:28,360
What about the people who work?

59
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:29,560
What is this?

60
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,950
What is this?

61
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:34,240
Next, for this sketch,

62
00:04:34,510 --> 00:04:35,630
the announcer and singer

63
00:04:35,630 --> 00:04:37,360
will be played by this old lady alone.

64
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:38,270
Hope you like it.

65
00:04:38,270 --> 00:04:38,870
Thank you.

66
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,240
This... This is called a pratfall.

67
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:42,310
I'll start singing.

68
00:04:42,310 --> 00:04:43,870
No floral fragrance.

69
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:10,630
Alright, alright.

70
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:11,390
Alright.

71
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:12,240
That's enough.

72
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:12,680
You sing a line.

73
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:13,680
-Come on.
-I... I...

74
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:15,120
Xiaozao, Xiaozao, Xiaozao.

75
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,000
I can't sing.

76
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:16,600
Sit down quickly.

77
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:17,600
Sit down, sit down.

78
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:18,160
Okay.

79
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:18,910
And this.

80
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,390
No need.

81
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:21,240
Sit.

82
00:05:21,850 --> 00:05:22,510
Have a seat.

83
00:05:22,750 --> 00:05:24,930
Is this what you usually do at auditions?

84
00:05:24,930 --> 00:05:26,330
This is my signature act.

85
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:28,240
I only bring it out for special occasions.

86
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:30,450
When I was a kid, during the 15-day
Spring Festival holiday,

87
00:05:30,450 --> 00:05:31,630
I'd put on

88
00:05:31,630 --> 00:05:34,150
a huge show for my whole family.

89
00:05:34,950 --> 00:05:35,720
That's nice.

90
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:41,970
Stop thinking about it.

91
00:05:42,190 --> 00:05:43,870
The most important thing for us right now

92
00:05:43,870 --> 00:05:45,200
is to solve the problem.

93
00:05:45,250 --> 00:05:46,630
And you're not all by yourself.

94
00:05:46,630 --> 00:05:48,490
You've still got us, haven't you?

95
00:05:50,210 --> 00:05:51,810
Leave your brother's matter

96
00:05:51,970 --> 00:05:53,970
to me, his younger brother-in-law,

97
00:05:54,290 --> 00:05:55,170
Ximei,

98
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,120
your younger brother's cousin,

99
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:59,120
and her boyfriend, Chen Junnan.

100
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:02,100
It will be fine.

101
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:08,570
Oh no! Oh no!

102
00:06:08,750 --> 00:06:09,350
He's gone!

103
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:10,190
Who?

104
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:10,830
Who?

105
00:06:10,830 --> 00:06:11,430
Jiahao.

106
00:06:11,460 --> 00:06:12,070
Where is he?

107
00:06:12,070 --> 00:06:13,950
Weren't you supposed
to keep an eye on him?

108
00:06:13,950 --> 00:06:16,210
He jumped off the second-floor balcony.

109
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:18,560
Jiahao!

110
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:19,480
Jiahao!

111
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:20,360
Jiahao!

112
00:06:20,390 --> 00:06:21,040
Jiahao!

113
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:22,950
Jiahao.

114
00:06:22,970 --> 00:06:24,370
Have you seen my brother?

115
00:06:24,870 --> 00:06:25,600
He's not here.

116
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:26,560
He's not here.

117
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:27,680
Did you find him?

118
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:28,600
No.

119
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:29,240
No?

120
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:34,360
Thanks.

121
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:35,430
Let's split up and keep looking.

122
00:06:35,430 --> 00:06:36,630
I'll look over there.

123
00:06:37,190 --> 00:06:38,120
We'll look over there.

124
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:38,510
Okay.

125
00:06:38,630 --> 00:06:39,310
Thanks.

126
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:42,120
Jiahao!

127
00:06:48,190 --> 00:06:49,600
-Jiahao!
-Jiahao!

128
00:06:49,630 --> 00:06:50,560
Jiahao!

129
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:51,510
Jiahao!

130
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:54,150
Jiahao!

131
00:06:54,630 --> 00:06:56,630
-Jiahao!
-Jiahao!

132
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:58,000
Jiahao!

133
00:07:06,190 --> 00:07:07,190
Jiahao!

134
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:10,300
What are you doing?

135
00:07:24,950 --> 00:07:25,510
Jiahao!

136
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:27,830
Zhou Ke, come back!

137
00:07:37,780 --> 00:07:39,330
Someone fell in the water over there!

138
00:07:39,330 --> 00:07:41,330
Move forward! Move forward!

139
00:07:42,510 --> 00:07:43,310
Where?

140
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:44,630
Over there!

141
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:46,040
Hurry!

142
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:47,630
Over there!

143
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,070
Hurry! Hurry!

144
00:07:51,150 --> 00:07:51,950
Over there!

145
00:07:51,950 --> 00:07:52,870
Here!

146
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,440
There!

147
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:10,500
So this is what heaven looks like.

148
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:12,480
Ke.

149
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,160
You're awake.

150
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:15,510
Ximei.

151
00:08:16,310 --> 00:08:17,360
You died, too?

152
00:08:18,390 --> 00:08:19,630
You're the one who died.

153
00:08:19,630 --> 00:08:21,160
No, you didn't die, either.

154
00:08:21,510 --> 00:08:22,600
Who saved me?

155
00:08:23,010 --> 00:08:24,200
Who else could it be?

156
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:25,490
Are you okay?

157
00:08:28,310 --> 00:08:29,070
Thank you.

158
00:08:29,750 --> 00:08:30,550
It's nothing.

159
00:08:33,630 --> 00:08:34,480
Where's Jiahao?

160
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,120
Is he okay?

161
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:35,909
He's fine.

162
00:08:35,909 --> 00:08:36,909
He's in his room.

163
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:40,480
Stop crying. Wipe your tears.

164
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:23,050
Look at you. You're a grown man,

165
00:09:23,150 --> 00:09:24,960
and now you're trying to kill yourself?

166
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:26,220
Aren't you something?

167
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:28,480
And you said

168
00:09:29,250 --> 00:09:30,480
we'd meet at the top.

169
00:09:31,550 --> 00:09:33,810
Well, we certainly met in the wind today.

170
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,750
Do you know how strong
the wind is outside?

171
00:09:35,750 --> 00:09:37,680
Look at how the wind blew us around.

172
00:09:38,850 --> 00:09:41,190
[Did Zhen ask you to come?]

173
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:42,670
I went out to sea today,

174
00:09:42,750 --> 00:09:44,550
and I just happened
to run into your drama.

175
00:09:44,550 --> 00:09:46,120
I only go out to sea twice a year.

176
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:47,780
How do I keep running into you?

177
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,810
Did you do it on purpose?

178
00:09:51,350 --> 00:09:53,930
And that time you got bitten by a goose,

179
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,000
got hit by a car,

180
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,790
and whatever happened in
that sugarcane field...

181
00:09:57,790 --> 00:09:59,590
I think you did it all on purpose.

182
00:10:03,630 --> 00:10:06,930
[Go back. I'm fine.]

183
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:07,480
All right, come out now.

184
00:10:08,570 --> 00:10:09,670
As for your little problem,

185
00:10:09,670 --> 00:10:10,790
everyone knows about it.

186
00:10:10,790 --> 00:10:12,200
So what if you got scammed
out of some money?

187
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,320
It's no big deal.

188
00:10:16,670 --> 00:10:18,550
Before my ex-husband died,

189
00:10:19,830 --> 00:10:21,690
he was scammed out of 200 million.

190
00:10:21,890 --> 00:10:23,890
I'm paying it back slowly, aren't I?

191
00:10:26,270 --> 00:10:27,400
You owe 200 million?

192
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:29,820
You really believe everything I say.

193
00:10:31,270 --> 00:10:32,290
You're already out.

194
00:10:32,290 --> 00:10:33,690
Why are you going back in?

195
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:40,150
Look at you.

196
00:10:41,030 --> 00:10:42,310
You look like a wreck.

197
00:10:43,340 --> 00:10:44,410
Looking at the state you're in,

198
00:10:44,410 --> 00:10:46,610
who'd want to spend their life with you?

199
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:51,910
Sorry for the trouble.

200
00:10:52,510 --> 00:10:54,110
You didn't cause me trouble.

201
00:10:56,510 --> 00:10:58,120
You caused Zhen trouble,

202
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:58,960
you know?

203
00:10:59,670 --> 00:11:02,000
It's one thing if you get yourself killed,

204
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:03,270
but did you even think about her

205
00:11:03,270 --> 00:11:04,440
You want to let her carry

206
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:05,900
all the things by herself?

207
00:11:06,510 --> 00:11:07,790
She is so young.

208
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:11,280
But you want to let her
carry so much by herself?

209
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:13,090
Have you ever thought about it?

210
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,520
Dying is the easy part.

211
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:22,920
Do you know how hard it is for the living?

212
00:11:25,410 --> 00:11:28,600
♪ Lost in the crowds, we carry on ♪

213
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:29,720
So how much have you paid back now?

214
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:32,120
♪ Someone will stay
with you through day and night ♪

215
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:34,000
Why can't I get through to you?

216
00:11:33,070 --> 00:11:36,390
♪ The art of loving and being loved ♪

217
00:11:36,610 --> 00:11:40,210
♪ I'll give my all
to get it right for you ♪

218
00:11:39,790 --> 00:11:40,750
I'm sorry.

219
00:11:41,270 --> 00:11:42,630
Don't say sorry to me.

220
00:11:41,470 --> 00:11:44,710
♪ Who would risk it all for you? ♪

221
00:11:43,150 --> 00:11:44,960
Say sorry to Zhen.

222
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:48,290
♪ Locking all the sorrow deep inside ♪

223
00:11:48,710 --> 00:11:52,440
♪ Like a clown who can become ♪

224
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:57,070
♪ The superhero who makes you smile ♪

225
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,540
Hello, Chief Fang.

226
00:11:56,870 --> 00:11:57,790
You're just passing by?

227
00:11:57,790 --> 00:11:58,320
Right.

228
00:11:58,030 --> 00:12:00,960
♪ Oh, time ♪

229
00:12:00,980 --> 00:12:04,780
♪ People who live like clowns ♪

230
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:03,640
I'll leave him to you.

231
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:07,960
♪ Have long forgotten the dust
on their sleeves ♪

232
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:07,200
We'll see you out.

233
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:08,120
I... I'll see her out.

234
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:13,460
♪ With honest hearts,
we make this world more tender ♪

235
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:08,960
We... we'll go see her out.

236
00:12:09,150 --> 00:12:11,080
Director Fang Hua, my name is Ximei.

237
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:12,610
You look really beautiful.

238
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:17,150
♪ Oh, time ♪

239
00:12:13,510 --> 00:12:14,390
You look like Qiuya.

240
00:12:14,390 --> 00:12:15,320
So pretty.

241
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:21,340
♪ We who were once loved by clowns ♪

242
00:12:21,850 --> 00:12:24,160
♪ Can become superheroes too ♪

243
00:12:24,190 --> 00:12:29,610
♪ Saving every inch of sorrow ♪

244
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:33,980
♪ Then the world is whole again ♪

245
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:37,030
What does this mean?

246
00:12:38,120 --> 00:12:40,380
You'll manage your own money from now on.

247
00:12:49,780 --> 00:12:52,980
♪ Lost in the crowds, we carry on ♪

248
00:12:53,230 --> 00:12:56,590
♪ Someone will stay
with you through day and night ♪

249
00:12:57,520 --> 00:13:01,120
♪ The art of loving and being loved ♪

250
00:13:01,650 --> 00:13:05,230
♪ I'll give my all
to get it right for you ♪

251
00:13:03,670 --> 00:13:05,200
Are you abandoning me?

252
00:13:05,870 --> 00:13:07,000
No.

253
00:13:06,330 --> 00:13:09,480
♪ Who would risk it all for you? ♪

254
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:09,630
I mean, from now on,

255
00:13:09,730 --> 00:13:13,230
♪ Locking all the sorrow deep inside ♪

256
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,200
we'll take care of our family together.

257
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,630
I'm sorry, Jiahao.

258
00:13:13,450 --> 00:13:17,980
♪ Like a clown who can become ♪

259
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:21,810
♪ The superhero who makes you smile ♪

260
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:20,630
What are you sorry for?

261
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:24,000
I should be the one saying sorry to you.

262
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:25,480
♪ Oh, time ♪

263
00:13:24,510 --> 00:13:25,630
It's all my fault.

264
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:29,370
♪ People who live like clowns ♪

265
00:13:25,910 --> 00:13:28,170
I shouldn't have always controlled you.

266
00:13:29,830 --> 00:13:32,480
♪ Have long forgotten the dust
on their sleeves ♪

267
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:32,440
If you hadn't kept me in check,

268
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:34,600
who knows how much trouble I'd cause?

269
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:38,160
♪ With honest hearts,
we make this world more tender ♪

270
00:13:35,550 --> 00:13:38,330
Even with you keeping me in check,
I still made so many mistakes.

271
00:13:38,330 --> 00:13:41,980
♪ Oh, time ♪

272
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:39,670
I'm sorry, Zhen.

273
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:43,120
I shouldn't have always
made decisions for you either.

274
00:13:42,180 --> 00:13:46,050
♪ We who were once loved by clowns ♪

275
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:44,750
I'm sorry.

276
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:46,600
If you didn't make decisions for me,

277
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:48,670
I wouldn't even know
how to live every day.

278
00:13:46,690 --> 00:13:49,080
♪ Can become superheroes too ♪

279
00:13:49,250 --> 00:13:54,530
♪ Saving every inch of sorrow ♪

280
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:51,270
So you still have to
make decisions for me.

281
00:13:51,270 --> 00:13:52,390
I'm sorry, Zhen.

282
00:13:53,550 --> 00:13:55,790
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have

283
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:57,960
♪ Oh, time ♪

284
00:13:57,150 --> 00:13:58,960
ignored your feelings. I...

285
00:13:58,190 --> 00:14:01,860
♪ People who live like clowns ♪

286
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,600
It's all my fault.

287
00:14:00,790 --> 00:14:01,720
No, it's mine.

288
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,000
I shouldn't have

289
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:05,570
♪ Have long forgotten the dust
on their sleeves ♪

290
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,000
disobeyed you
when you tried to keep me in check,

291
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,360
because everything you said was right.

292
00:14:05,890 --> 00:14:11,250
♪ With honest hearts,
we make this world more tender ♪

293
00:14:09,750 --> 00:14:12,670
I...

294
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:15,070
♪ Oh, time ♪

295
00:14:13,670 --> 00:14:14,080
What's wrong?

296
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:17,030
I almost lost my brother.

297
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:19,150
♪ We who were once loved by clowns ♪

298
00:14:17,910 --> 00:14:19,720
Brother, I'm sorry

299
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:22,170
♪ Can become superheroes too ♪

300
00:14:22,350 --> 00:14:27,620
♪ Saving every inch of sorrow ♪

301
00:14:22,510 --> 00:14:25,150
I almost lost my sister too.

302
00:14:25,570 --> 00:14:27,830
I shouldn't have always controlled you.

303
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,020
You have to control me.

304
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:33,990
♪ Then the world is whole again ♪

305
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:31,480
I can't do
without you keeping me in check.

306
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:33,270
I won't control you anymore.

307
00:14:33,270 --> 00:14:36,470
How am I supposed to manage
without you keeping me in line?

308
00:14:56,480 --> 00:14:58,680
I thought about it all night last night.

309
00:14:59,870 --> 00:15:01,730
I'm not going to run away anymore.

310
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:04,760
The most urgent thing
is how to face the villagers.

311
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:07,430
I've thought it through.

312
00:15:07,750 --> 00:15:09,670
I'll go door to door
and get down on my knees.

313
00:15:09,670 --> 00:15:10,270
No, no, no.

314
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:11,650
The most important thing now

315
00:15:11,650 --> 00:15:13,450
is how to pay the villagers back.

316
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:16,170
I've really thought this through.

317
00:15:16,450 --> 00:15:17,720
I'm going to borrow from a loan shark.

318
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:18,200
No, no, no.

319
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:19,670
You haven't thought it through.
Think again.

320
00:15:19,670 --> 00:15:20,410
Ke, say something.

321
00:15:20,410 --> 00:15:22,870
There's actually one thing
I haven't figured out.

322
00:15:22,870 --> 00:15:25,130
Don't you think this scammer is too good?

323
00:15:25,290 --> 00:15:26,890
He knows you guys inside out.

324
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,760
He even had a photo with your dad.

325
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:31,510
That

326
00:15:31,510 --> 00:15:32,420
was AI-generated.

327
00:15:32,420 --> 00:15:34,030
Then he must at least have a photo, right?

328
00:15:34,030 --> 00:15:34,440
Besides,

329
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:35,120
he knew all those things

330
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:36,150
about your dad.

331
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:39,410
You mean it was an inside job?

332
00:15:40,070 --> 00:15:42,130
It's very likely someone very close.

333
00:15:45,870 --> 00:15:46,750
No, why are you looking at her?

334
00:15:46,750 --> 00:15:48,030
How could it be her?
You're looking at her.

335
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:48,960
I didn't mean it is my sister.

336
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:49,840
-Then why are you looking at her?
-I didn't mean...

337
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:50,510
I meant...

338
00:15:52,340 --> 00:15:53,670
Well, here's the thing.

339
00:15:54,390 --> 00:15:55,600
In his story,

340
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:57,440
there was always someone

341
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:58,910
who has now disappeared.

342
00:15:59,080 --> 00:15:59,750
Who?

343
00:16:01,390 --> 00:16:03,590
I'm not saying this because I'm biased,

344
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,600
or because I have
personal feelings about this,

345
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,730
or because I'm being petty.

346
00:16:07,750 --> 00:16:08,780
You mean Bingqiang?

347
00:16:08,780 --> 00:16:09,380
Yes.

348
00:16:09,890 --> 00:16:10,800
Impossible.

349
00:16:11,550 --> 00:16:13,960
Bingqiang was the first one to worry
about me being scammed.

350
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:15,750
He even checked the website for me online.

351
00:16:15,750 --> 00:16:16,240
Look.

352
00:16:16,630 --> 00:16:17,790
That website was fake.

353
00:16:17,790 --> 00:16:20,120
How did it show up
as real when he searched?

354
00:16:20,870 --> 00:16:21,440
No.

355
00:16:21,670 --> 00:16:23,020
What's his motive for doing this?

356
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:23,840
This is impossible.

357
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,200
We grew up together.

358
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:25,720
How could he...

359
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:27,240
Why would he hurt us?

360
00:16:27,550 --> 00:16:29,270
From an acting perspective,

361
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:31,000
a character's backstory

362
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:33,330
has a huge impact on what happens next.

363
00:16:33,620 --> 00:16:34,860
When he was young,

364
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:36,750
he watched the whole village

365
00:16:36,750 --> 00:16:38,210
send his father to prison.

366
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:39,750
Wouldn't that leave a lasting mark on him?

367
00:16:39,750 --> 00:16:41,150
Wouldn't he resent them?

368
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:43,600
Even if he holds a grudge,

369
00:16:43,790 --> 00:16:45,620
he wouldn't take it out on us.

370
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:47,360
The three of us grew up...

371
00:16:48,760 --> 00:16:49,310
I...

372
00:16:49,870 --> 00:16:50,680
You eat.

373
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:52,850
I have to call him.

374
00:16:56,980 --> 00:16:57,790
Sorry.

375
00:16:57,910 --> 00:17:00,240
The subscriber you dialed is powered off.

376
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:02,200
It's powered off.

377
00:17:04,589 --> 00:17:07,200
Attention, all villagers,

378
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:09,390
please go to the village committee
for a meeting.

379
00:17:09,390 --> 00:17:11,910
Attention, all villagers,

380
00:17:11,930 --> 00:17:14,660
please go to the village committee
for a meeting.

381
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:25,920
Stop arguing!

382
00:17:28,720 --> 00:17:31,520
I've only been away
from the village for a few days,

383
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:33,620
and such a big thing happened.

384
00:17:34,790 --> 00:17:36,590
When I heard the news out of town,

385
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:39,550
I was so anxious I couldn't speak.

386
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:42,720
I-I rushed back overnight.

387
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:46,270
You, Jiahao,

388
00:17:47,160 --> 00:17:48,160
did I wrong you?

389
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:50,000
Am I right?

390
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,790
You are just a hopeless case.

391
00:18:03,750 --> 00:18:04,810
Fellow villagers,

392
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:09,680
since the police
have finished investigating,

393
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:12,000
we should trust them.

394
00:18:13,270 --> 00:18:14,360
Besides,

395
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:15,720
we watched

396
00:18:16,350 --> 00:18:18,960
Jiahao grow up.

397
00:18:19,510 --> 00:18:22,440
We all know what kind of person he is,

398
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:23,680
right?

399
00:18:24,290 --> 00:18:26,450
He's not a bad person.

400
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:29,330
He's just stupid.

401
00:18:30,520 --> 00:18:31,200
Yes.

402
00:18:33,200 --> 00:18:34,260
Fellow villagers,

403
00:18:35,310 --> 00:18:37,960
a person must take responsibility
for their own actions.

404
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,110
I'll take full responsibility

405
00:18:39,110 --> 00:18:41,000
for this matter.

406
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:43,450
How can you take responsibility?

407
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:44,460
Do you have money?

408
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:45,480
Do you have that kind of money?

409
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:47,420
I will definitely find a way
to pay everyone back.

410
00:18:47,420 --> 00:18:48,730
Money, money, money.

411
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:50,410
Where is the money?

412
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:56,070
Zhen and I have already discussed it.

413
00:18:56,070 --> 00:18:57,730
We are going to sell the house.

414
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:01,790
How much is your rundown house worth?

415
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,830
Do you know how much money that is?

416
00:19:04,830 --> 00:19:06,480
That's a huge sum of money.

417
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:08,680
How can you bear it alone?

418
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:10,510
Uncle Huixian,

419
00:19:10,510 --> 00:19:12,170
what do you think we should do?

420
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:17,940
Fellow villagers,

421
00:19:19,110 --> 00:19:21,200
on my way back yesterday,

422
00:19:21,590 --> 00:19:23,030
someone reached out to me

423
00:19:23,790 --> 00:19:27,070
and said he could help us.

424
00:19:28,270 --> 00:19:29,440
Next,

425
00:19:29,790 --> 00:19:32,110
I'll let you

426
00:19:32,310 --> 00:19:34,550
decide for yourselves, okay?

427
00:19:34,570 --> 00:19:35,770
How do we choose?

428
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:39,270
T-That's it.

429
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:48,790
Hello,

430
00:19:49,030 --> 00:19:50,090
fellow villagers.

431
00:19:51,070 --> 00:19:52,200
My surname is Huang.

432
00:19:52,310 --> 00:19:53,690
I am an entrepreneur.

433
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:55,040
Our group heard

434
00:19:55,070 --> 00:19:56,590
about what happened

435
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:58,360
to you while we were
looking for a site nearby.

436
00:19:58,360 --> 00:19:59,960
Seeing what happened to you,

437
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:01,510
I was deeply concerned.

438
00:20:01,510 --> 00:20:03,200
I am also a child of farmers,

439
00:20:03,350 --> 00:20:06,240
so I know your money is hard-earned.

440
00:20:06,770 --> 00:20:08,210
I feel deep sympathy

441
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:09,970
for what you have been through.

442
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,030
So, all the shareholders of the group

443
00:20:13,030 --> 00:20:14,490
held an overnight meeting

444
00:20:14,660 --> 00:20:17,390
and finalized
all the compensation agreements.

445
00:20:17,590 --> 00:20:21,750
As long as everyone agrees
to the demolition,

446
00:20:22,070 --> 00:20:23,240
I'll personally cover 50%

447
00:20:23,240 --> 00:20:25,270
of your financial losses!

448
00:20:25,750 --> 00:20:28,270
Look.

449
00:20:34,270 --> 00:20:35,670
This is my business card!

450
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,310
Ma Group?

451
00:20:40,790 --> 00:20:41,990
How do we contact him?

452
00:20:44,750 --> 00:20:46,750
Fellow villagers, don't be fooled.

453
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,830
He's Mr. Huang from Ma Construction Group,

454
00:20:48,830 --> 00:20:50,600
the one who wanted
to demolish our village before.

455
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:53,730
Those bad guys,
Gao Jiaoqi and Fei, were working for him.

456
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:55,000
He's a bad guy.

457
00:20:58,040 --> 00:20:58,510
Well...

458
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:01,050
I admit it. I admit it all.

459
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:01,960
See? He admitted it.

460
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:03,690
But let me make one thing clear.

461
00:21:03,770 --> 00:21:05,820
Gao Jiaoqi, our former employee,

462
00:21:06,270 --> 00:21:08,070
was responsible for all of this.

463
00:21:08,510 --> 00:21:09,510
It was shameful.

464
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:11,640
I've already fired him,

465
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:14,920
and I apologize
to everyone on his behalf.

466
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:19,060
-Apologizing is useless.
-Exactly.

467
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:20,750
Listen.

468
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:23,290
I can completely understand how you feel.

469
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:25,350
But you need

470
00:21:25,680 --> 00:21:26,830
to get the money

471
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:28,710
in your pockets first.

472
00:21:29,510 --> 00:21:31,710
If you agree to sell your houses to us...

473
00:21:31,790 --> 00:21:34,480
We genuinely want to help you all.

474
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:35,880
If you want to sell your houses

475
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:37,310
to our group,

476
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:39,440
just go to him, okay?

477
00:21:39,790 --> 00:21:41,440
My name is Gao Jiaoba.

478
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:44,730
Anyone looking to sell their house,
come to me

479
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:45,400
and sign up.

480
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:46,310
Good!

481
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:55,480
No rush.

482
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:56,960
Talk to him.

483
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:57,750
Talk to him.

484
00:21:57,750 --> 00:22:00,010
Get in line, everyone. One line, please.

485
00:22:02,750 --> 00:22:04,640
There's definitely something wrong
with Mr. Huang.

486
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,830
Otherwise, why would he
be willing to pay

487
00:22:05,830 --> 00:22:07,360
so much money for no reason?

488
00:22:09,900 --> 00:22:11,930
There's definitely something wrong
with Mr. Huang.

489
00:22:11,930 --> 00:22:14,170
Jiahao, didn't I just say that?

490
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:17,880
Why would he give us

491
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:19,050
so much money for no reason?

492
00:22:19,050 --> 00:22:21,160
We already talked about that, too.
What were you thinking about?

493
00:22:21,160 --> 00:22:22,200
I zoned out.

494
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:25,380
There's definitely
something fishy about him.

495
00:22:26,270 --> 00:22:28,530
But we don't have any evidence right now.

496
00:22:31,110 --> 00:22:32,880
Look at this ping-pong table.
Pretty nice, huh?

497
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:34,240
I could put it in my office

498
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:35,310
and use it as a tea table.

499
00:22:35,310 --> 00:22:37,590
We don't need this chair. It's too old.

500
00:22:38,250 --> 00:22:39,380
Burn it for a stew.

501
00:22:40,340 --> 00:22:41,420
Look at this view.

502
00:22:41,580 --> 00:22:42,380
Look.

503
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:44,000
What a great view.

504
00:22:44,020 --> 00:22:44,630
Right.

505
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:47,250
We'll build a public restroom right here.

506
00:22:47,350 --> 00:22:48,830
This exact scene...

507
00:22:48,830 --> 00:22:50,310
I've thought about this.

508
00:22:50,450 --> 00:22:51,000
Right here.

509
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:52,590
What would we put here?

510
00:22:52,610 --> 00:22:54,640
This section will have seated toilets.

511
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,110
What about here?

512
00:22:55,110 --> 00:22:55,830
Squat toilets.

513
00:22:55,830 --> 00:22:56,480
And here?

514
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:57,310
Urinals.

515
00:22:57,330 --> 00:22:58,130
Great.

516
00:22:58,880 --> 00:23:00,480
Then we squat down right here

517
00:23:01,750 --> 00:23:03,080
and make our last stand.

518
00:23:03,440 --> 00:23:04,400
Are you stupid?

519
00:23:04,640 --> 00:23:05,550
Turn around.

520
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:10,510
A sea-view restroom!

521
00:23:10,750 --> 00:23:12,880
Wait, what exactly are you guys doing?

522
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:14,640
Why are you in the toilet?

523
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:16,790
Wait, there are people here?

524
00:23:18,790 --> 00:23:20,750
You haven't left yet?

525
00:23:21,050 --> 00:23:23,330
Go sign up with Jiaoba.

526
00:23:23,370 --> 00:23:24,940
How can you take advantage of people
when they're down?

527
00:23:24,940 --> 00:23:26,890
Young man, watch your mouth.

528
00:23:27,300 --> 00:23:28,920
Don't make false accusations.
I'll sue you.

529
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:29,920
Can you handle it?

530
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:30,990
Excuse me.

531
00:23:31,010 --> 00:23:32,750
Until the demolition goes ahead,
this is still private property.

532
00:23:32,750 --> 00:23:34,380
You are not welcome here. Leave now.

533
00:23:34,380 --> 00:23:35,480
-Go.
-He's right. Leave now.

534
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:36,080
Zhou Ke.

535
00:23:37,310 --> 00:23:39,030
You lousy extra,

536
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:41,370
stop acting like you're the star
of the show.

537
00:23:41,370 --> 00:23:43,570
Could you leave out the insult, please?

538
00:23:43,570 --> 00:23:44,240
Fine.

539
00:23:44,970 --> 00:23:46,050
A plain old extra.

540
00:23:46,510 --> 00:23:47,710
Right, right, right.

541
00:23:48,280 --> 00:23:49,080
Zhen.

542
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:50,750
You're so pretty.

543
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:52,350
Why are you so dumb?

544
00:23:52,490 --> 00:23:53,110
Who are you talking about?

545
00:23:53,110 --> 00:23:54,160
Look at Jiahao.

546
00:23:54,510 --> 00:23:55,640
He's got the full set—

547
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:56,880
no looks, no charm,

548
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:57,880
no brains.

549
00:23:58,530 --> 00:23:59,830
He heard "Follow Chris"

550
00:23:59,830 --> 00:24:00,640
and just followed him.

551
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:02,240
If you two have nothing to do—

552
00:24:03,110 --> 00:24:05,170
How do you know Chris's catchphrase?

553
00:24:09,350 --> 00:24:11,200
Stop talking about following this or that.

554
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:13,270
You'll be saying goodbye
to this place soon.

555
00:24:13,270 --> 00:24:14,310
Give it a rest.

556
00:24:15,910 --> 00:24:16,950
What are you doing?

557
00:24:16,950 --> 00:24:17,980
Mr. Huang,

558
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:20,200
I know your surname,

559
00:24:20,220 --> 00:24:21,830
but I don't know your first name,

560
00:24:21,830 --> 00:24:23,960
so I guess I'll just call you Mr. Huang.

561
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:25,350
You are a bad guy.

562
00:24:25,480 --> 00:24:28,200
I know you're tearing down the village

563
00:24:28,230 --> 00:24:29,890
just to get at the treasure
buried underneath it.

564
00:24:29,890 --> 00:24:31,640
As long as I'm here,

565
00:24:31,930 --> 00:24:34,300
I'll find the treasure before you do.

566
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:36,240
Mr. Huang

567
00:24:37,120 --> 00:24:38,190
is a bad guy.

568
00:24:40,910 --> 00:24:42,180
Are you crazy?

569
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:44,700
I'll tear this whole place down later!

570
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:46,390
Watch your mouth.

571
00:24:49,110 --> 00:24:50,590
Look for the treasure carefully.

572
00:24:50,590 --> 00:24:51,240
Let me know

573
00:24:51,640 --> 00:24:52,920
when you find it.

574
00:24:53,070 --> 00:24:53,480
Take care when stepping.

575
00:24:53,480 --> 00:24:55,280
Don't break the seated toilets.

576
00:25:06,220 --> 00:25:06,830
Jiahao,

577
00:25:07,320 --> 00:25:08,720
are you sure you haven't

578
00:25:08,720 --> 00:25:10,650
told anyone about "Follow Chris"?

579
00:25:10,660 --> 00:25:11,860
I'm very sure.

580
00:25:12,270 --> 00:25:13,960
I've only told you guys

581
00:25:13,980 --> 00:25:15,440
and the police about this.

582
00:25:16,160 --> 00:25:18,090
Then this is getting interesting.

583
00:25:27,140 --> 00:25:27,860
How is it?

584
00:25:28,210 --> 00:25:29,450
I looked into things.

585
00:25:30,550 --> 00:25:32,590
Pretty much everyone has signed.

586
00:25:33,270 --> 00:25:34,160
Everyone?

587
00:25:34,750 --> 00:25:35,410
Basically.

588
00:25:41,510 --> 00:25:43,270
Is there any other way now?

589
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:46,050
We've gotten through so much before.

590
00:25:46,050 --> 00:25:48,250
This time, it is different from before.

591
00:25:48,640 --> 00:25:49,880
Now we have no grounds

592
00:25:50,030 --> 00:25:51,830
to ask the villagers not to sign.

593
00:25:53,200 --> 00:25:55,070
The villagers won't listen to us, either.

594
00:25:55,070 --> 00:25:56,240
So the demolition

595
00:25:57,640 --> 00:25:59,100
is pretty much a done deal.

596
00:26:04,880 --> 00:26:06,510
But we can't let them
tear the village down like this.

597
00:26:06,510 --> 00:26:07,910
He swindled their money,

598
00:26:08,160 --> 00:26:09,490
then played the good guy

599
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:11,480
while tearing their homes down anyway.

600
00:26:11,480 --> 00:26:12,750
The villagers still suffered losses.

601
00:26:12,750 --> 00:26:14,200
They'd have been better off
with the original demolition deal.

602
00:26:14,200 --> 00:26:14,880
Right.

603
00:26:16,270 --> 00:26:17,310
The priority is

604
00:26:17,640 --> 00:26:18,700
to figure out a way.

605
00:26:18,960 --> 00:26:20,480
If the village gets demolished,

606
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:21,680
we need to find a way
to make him cough up

607
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:23,740
the money he swindled from everyone.

608
00:26:23,850 --> 00:26:25,680
Right. Make him cough it up.

609
00:26:26,820 --> 00:26:27,530
But how?

610
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:30,310
The problem is, we don't know

611
00:26:30,310 --> 00:26:32,180
what Mr. Huang's weak spot is.

612
00:26:32,790 --> 00:26:33,790
For example...

613
00:26:35,310 --> 00:26:37,170
How about I use a honey trap on him?

614
00:26:37,690 --> 00:26:38,340
I...

615
00:26:40,110 --> 00:26:40,680
No way.

616
00:26:42,030 --> 00:26:42,830
I disagree.

617
00:26:43,710 --> 00:26:44,510
How about I...

618
00:26:44,670 --> 00:26:45,360
No.

619
00:26:46,160 --> 00:26:46,590
No.

620
00:26:47,090 --> 00:26:48,020
I also disagree.

621
00:26:50,320 --> 00:26:51,120
Let me do it.

622
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:53,930
A honey trap?

623
00:26:54,090 --> 00:26:54,750
You?

624
00:26:56,480 --> 00:26:57,810
I'll sacrifice myself.

625
00:26:59,960 --> 00:27:01,690
I'll find someone to kidnap him

626
00:27:01,960 --> 00:27:03,890
and force him to pay the money back.

627
00:27:04,790 --> 00:27:06,050
I'll sacrifice myself

628
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:08,580
for the good of the whole village.

629
00:27:10,200 --> 00:27:11,070
Great.

630
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:12,940
I've been looking
for my next man for ages.

631
00:27:12,940 --> 00:27:13,460
Go quickly.

632
00:27:13,460 --> 00:27:14,060
Forget it.

633
00:27:15,110 --> 00:27:16,600
Let's think about it again.

634
00:27:16,600 --> 00:27:18,030
That's just nonsense.

635
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:21,770
I actually have an idea.

636
00:27:24,070 --> 00:27:25,600
I don't know if it will work.

637
00:27:27,030 --> 00:27:29,110
So here's my plan:

638
00:27:29,160 --> 00:27:30,910
find someone Mr. Huang doesn't know

639
00:27:30,910 --> 00:27:32,910
to pose as a potential investor

640
00:27:33,230 --> 00:27:35,080
interested in our village

641
00:27:35,600 --> 00:27:37,440
and force Mr. Huang
to up his offer.

642
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:39,020
Then the extra money can
go to the villagers.

643
00:27:39,020 --> 00:27:41,180
That way, he'd be coughing up
the money he swindled from them.

644
00:27:41,180 --> 00:27:42,380
Amazing! Awesome!

645
00:27:42,480 --> 00:27:44,610
What if Mr. Huang refuses
to up his offer?

646
00:27:44,610 --> 00:27:46,000
He put so much effort into it.

647
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:48,640
There's no way he'd just hand it over
to someone else over this amount of money.

648
00:27:48,640 --> 00:27:50,040
Right. It's impossible.

649
00:27:50,270 --> 00:27:51,790
This is all the villagers' information,
right?

650
00:27:51,790 --> 00:27:52,350
Yes.

651
00:27:52,510 --> 00:27:54,400
I organized this when I was

652
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:55,860
the acting village chief.

653
00:27:56,590 --> 00:27:58,370
But the villagers have already
signed the agreement.

654
00:27:58,370 --> 00:28:00,650
Will they agree to play along with us?

655
00:28:01,510 --> 00:28:02,420
Aren't we putting on this act

656
00:28:02,420 --> 00:28:03,810
to get a better deal

657
00:28:03,880 --> 00:28:04,960
for our villagers?

658
00:28:05,400 --> 00:28:06,680
Whether they cooperate or not,

659
00:28:06,680 --> 00:28:08,000
the problem now is,

660
00:28:08,480 --> 00:28:10,680
none of us really looks the part,

661
00:28:11,320 --> 00:28:13,640
and one slip-up could blow our cover.

662
00:28:16,330 --> 00:28:17,330
Then how about this?

663
00:28:17,330 --> 00:28:19,620
I'll transfer some professional actors
from Shudian.

664
00:28:19,620 --> 00:28:20,720
No, absolutely not.

665
00:28:20,720 --> 00:28:22,190
First, we're running out of time.

666
00:28:22,190 --> 00:28:23,020
We need to move fast.

667
00:28:23,020 --> 00:28:24,030
Otherwise, once they finish signing,

668
00:28:24,030 --> 00:28:25,200
it will be too late for everything.

669
00:28:25,200 --> 00:28:26,830
Second, it's too risky

670
00:28:27,070 --> 00:28:28,670
to hire someone to play a role

671
00:28:28,750 --> 00:28:29,750
in something like this.

672
00:28:29,750 --> 00:28:31,680
What if something else goes wrong?

673
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:38,310
Calm down.

674
00:28:38,310 --> 00:28:39,160
Let me think.

675
00:28:39,750 --> 00:28:41,790
We need someone Mr. Huang doesn't know,

676
00:28:41,790 --> 00:28:43,440
but whom we can trust.

677
00:28:43,480 --> 00:28:43,920
Right.

678
00:28:43,920 --> 00:28:47,310
Someone who can act,
and we need them here ASAP.

679
00:28:50,590 --> 00:28:51,030
Her.

680
00:28:51,640 --> 00:28:52,160
Who?

681
00:28:52,160 --> 00:28:52,680
Who?

682
00:28:52,720 --> 00:28:54,270
You, Lin Ximei.

683
00:28:56,690 --> 00:28:58,220
Mr. Huang doesn't know you.

684
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:05,110
Me?

685
00:29:05,790 --> 00:29:07,240
I can trust you, right?

686
00:29:10,800 --> 00:29:12,170
Ke, here's the thing.

687
00:29:12,200 --> 00:29:12,960
Handling men

688
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:14,440
is okay for me.

689
00:29:14,510 --> 00:29:16,700
But pulling that off in this situation?

690
00:29:16,700 --> 00:29:17,620
I can't do it.

691
00:29:19,530 --> 00:29:21,720
Ximei, don't try to handle another man.

692
00:29:21,720 --> 00:29:22,310
Shut up.

693
00:29:22,590 --> 00:29:24,320
Look at the situation we're in.

694
00:29:24,550 --> 00:29:25,790
If I could do it, I'd do it myself.

695
00:29:25,790 --> 00:29:27,250
But he knows me, so I can't.

696
00:29:27,350 --> 00:29:29,400
You're the only one
among us he doesn't know.

697
00:29:29,400 --> 00:29:31,590
I can't act.

698
00:29:32,960 --> 00:29:34,030
You're so good at handling people.

699
00:29:34,030 --> 00:29:35,110
How could your acting be bad?

700
00:29:35,110 --> 00:29:37,110
Besides, with our family's genes...

701
00:29:37,110 --> 00:29:38,110
And you've got me.

702
00:29:40,040 --> 00:29:42,440
Ximei, what we have
isn't just an act, is it?

703
00:29:45,330 --> 00:29:46,470
[Forever Love]

704
00:29:46,880 --> 00:29:47,810
Then it's a deal.

705
00:29:48,070 --> 00:29:49,070
No more nonsense.

706
00:29:49,410 --> 00:29:50,810
Let's get ready to start.

707
00:29:53,950 --> 00:29:55,400
This scene is crucial.

708
00:29:55,430 --> 00:29:56,430
We must act well.

709
00:29:56,480 --> 00:29:58,680
We have to work seamlessly as a team.

710
00:29:58,750 --> 00:30:00,110
Mr. Huang is very cunning.

711
00:30:00,110 --> 00:30:01,310
To make it convincing,

712
00:30:01,310 --> 00:30:02,750
he needs to see
the village chief and Ximei

713
00:30:02,750 --> 00:30:05,550
discussing a deal at the village committee
office with his own eyes.

714
00:30:05,550 --> 00:30:06,160
Go ahead.

715
00:30:06,790 --> 00:30:09,070
So how do we get Mr. Huang to show up
at just the right moment?

716
00:30:09,070 --> 00:30:09,930
Good question.

717
00:30:10,070 --> 00:30:12,830
That's where Shapu's
number-one tough guy,

718
00:30:12,830 --> 00:30:13,830
Junnan, comes in.

719
00:30:17,200 --> 00:30:17,800
Mr. Huang.

720
00:30:17,830 --> 00:30:18,720
Chen Junnan.

721
00:30:19,110 --> 00:30:21,140
You still have the nerve to video call me?

722
00:30:21,140 --> 00:30:22,600
Let me tell you something.

723
00:30:23,160 --> 00:30:25,400
Well, there's another boss

724
00:30:25,700 --> 00:30:28,230
who wants to buy our village now.
I'm serious.

725
00:30:28,570 --> 00:30:30,030
And they're offering more money.

726
00:30:30,030 --> 00:30:32,160
Why are you telling me this?

727
00:30:33,640 --> 00:30:36,200
I... I just want to come back to you.

728
00:30:36,250 --> 00:30:37,000
I just realized

729
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:38,720
there's no future with them.

730
00:30:38,740 --> 00:30:40,670
I might as well stick with you.

731
00:30:41,270 --> 00:30:42,440
I don't believe you.

732
00:30:42,540 --> 00:30:43,800
I'll... I'll show you.

733
00:30:45,750 --> 00:30:46,440
It's them.

734
00:30:49,190 --> 00:30:49,780
Yes.

735
00:30:51,350 --> 00:30:52,810
They just finished trying
to talk me into it.

736
00:30:52,810 --> 00:30:54,750
Now they're working
on the other villagers.

737
00:30:54,750 --> 00:30:56,410
But I didn't agree, Mr. Huang.

738
00:30:57,680 --> 00:30:59,850
Gao Jiaoba, get the car ready!

739
00:31:12,750 --> 00:31:14,000
Target is in position.

740
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:15,260
Everyone in position.

741
00:31:16,070 --> 00:31:16,790
Over.

742
00:31:17,300 --> 00:31:18,230
Got it.

743
00:31:21,580 --> 00:31:22,780
Mr. Huang, Mr. Huang.

744
00:31:23,160 --> 00:31:23,750
There you are.

745
00:31:23,750 --> 00:31:24,350
Where are they?

746
00:31:24,350 --> 00:31:25,240
They're at the village committee.

747
00:31:25,240 --> 00:31:26,300
This way, this way.

748
00:31:26,350 --> 00:31:27,240
It's... it's her.

749
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:28,220
How long has she been here?

750
00:31:28,220 --> 00:31:29,310
For a good few hours.

751
00:31:29,310 --> 00:31:29,960
Look.

752
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:31,530
Go ahead.

753
00:31:32,590 --> 00:31:33,960
But the village chief knows Ximei.

754
00:31:33,960 --> 00:31:35,400
Wouldn't that blow our cover?

755
00:31:35,400 --> 00:31:36,000
Good question.

756
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:37,200
So they absolutely cannot

757
00:31:37,200 --> 00:31:38,530
appear at the same time.

758
00:31:41,070 --> 00:31:42,550
Why are you dressed like that?

759
00:31:41,790 --> 00:31:44,770
[They are here]

760
00:31:43,550 --> 00:31:45,010
Something happened

761
00:31:45,550 --> 00:31:46,240
at home.

762
00:31:47,480 --> 00:31:48,160
What?

763
00:31:49,720 --> 00:31:51,070
My father passed away.

764
00:31:52,960 --> 00:31:53,750
That beautiful, elegant,

765
00:31:53,750 --> 00:31:54,830
and well-to-do woman

766
00:31:54,830 --> 00:31:55,640
is their boss.

767
00:31:56,270 --> 00:31:57,200
My condolences.

768
00:31:59,590 --> 00:32:00,640
So, did the deal go through,

769
00:32:00,640 --> 00:32:02,770
or did the chief
get together with her?

770
00:32:02,920 --> 00:32:04,180
It's gotta be the deal.

771
00:32:04,230 --> 00:32:05,750
It's gotta be the deal.

772
00:32:05,780 --> 00:32:06,740
I was just

773
00:32:07,270 --> 00:32:08,350
messing with you.

774
00:32:09,880 --> 00:32:11,310
Tonight, we have a...

775
00:32:11,310 --> 00:32:12,070
Look at them talking and laughing.

776
00:32:12,070 --> 00:32:13,310
Looks like they're close
to closing the deal, Mr. Huang.

777
00:32:13,310 --> 00:32:14,970
Let's go see what she's about.

778
00:32:15,350 --> 00:32:16,030
Okay?

779
00:32:16,030 --> 00:32:16,440
Yes.

780
00:32:17,040 --> 00:32:17,680
Go ahead.

781
00:32:18,440 --> 00:32:20,850
Won't Mr. Huang see through the act
if he gets too close?

782
00:32:20,850 --> 00:32:21,710
Good question.

783
00:32:21,720 --> 00:32:24,720
That's where our brave
and brilliant Jiahao comes in.

784
00:32:24,900 --> 00:32:25,490
Me?

785
00:32:25,570 --> 00:32:26,270
You scared me.

786
00:32:26,270 --> 00:32:28,330
My heart can't take much more of this.

787
00:32:28,350 --> 00:32:29,480
It's just the two of us
in the village committee,

788
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:31,680
Uncle Huixian!

789
00:32:32,350 --> 00:32:32,920
Oh no.

790
00:32:32,920 --> 00:32:33,270
What's wrong?

791
00:32:33,270 --> 00:32:35,070
Y-Your Seventh Aunt is missing.

792
00:32:36,310 --> 00:32:37,200
Then I'll go look for her first.

793
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:38,350
Go, go, go. Hurry, hurry.

794
00:32:38,350 --> 00:32:39,640
-Hey.
-Find Seventh Aunt.

795
00:32:39,640 --> 00:32:41,350
Go. Hurry. Let's go. Hurry, hurry.

796
00:32:41,350 --> 00:32:43,440
What are you yelling for? Seventh Aunt!

797
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:44,240
Seventh Aunt!

798
00:32:58,990 --> 00:33:02,120
Okay, getting Mr. Huang
in here is just the first step.

799
00:33:02,150 --> 00:33:04,350
Now comes the most important part:

800
00:33:04,440 --> 00:33:06,000
Ximei's performance.

801
00:33:06,320 --> 00:33:07,520
I'll just improvise.

802
00:33:08,170 --> 00:33:10,590
No, you can't improvise this time.

803
00:33:10,610 --> 00:33:12,110
We need to prepare thoroughly

804
00:33:12,110 --> 00:33:13,680
so we don't give ourselves away.

805
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:15,590
We need a complete character biography.

806
00:33:15,590 --> 00:33:16,350
First,

807
00:33:16,370 --> 00:33:17,410
who are you?

808
00:33:17,440 --> 00:33:18,160
Hi there.

809
00:33:18,160 --> 00:33:20,000
I am Jennifer Adele Gold.

810
00:33:20,030 --> 00:33:22,030
We need a company name that's obscure
enough to be hard to look up,

811
00:33:22,030 --> 00:33:23,290
but still believable.

812
00:33:23,350 --> 00:33:25,640
I am the CEO

813
00:33:25,640 --> 00:33:26,290
of Tudak Hills.

814
00:33:26,290 --> 00:33:29,220
Our company mainly deals
in tourism and real estate.

815
00:33:30,910 --> 00:33:32,560
They will search
your name online,

816
00:33:32,560 --> 00:33:34,220
but they won't find anything.

817
00:33:39,030 --> 00:33:39,680
Right.

818
00:33:39,680 --> 00:33:41,270
I just got back from overseas.

819
00:33:41,270 --> 00:33:42,790
I used to live in London.

820
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:46,070
Maybe... you can search me on Google.

821
00:33:46,310 --> 00:33:48,310
I'll ask Mr. Maling
to set up a fake website

822
00:33:48,310 --> 00:33:50,310
and put all your information on it.

823
00:33:50,790 --> 00:33:51,400
Okay.

824
00:33:58,470 --> 00:33:59,510
Have you seen it?

825
00:34:02,270 --> 00:34:04,730
The background
on this page is a little dark.

826
00:34:05,230 --> 00:34:08,159
It's because you're
wearing those huge sunglasses.

827
00:34:09,540 --> 00:34:10,270
I forgot.

828
00:34:11,679 --> 00:34:15,800
The text on your company website
is a little small.

829
00:34:15,820 --> 00:34:17,320
You should change it later.

830
00:34:17,320 --> 00:34:18,840
This is very important.

831
00:34:18,880 --> 00:34:20,090
We need not just character backstories,

832
00:34:20,090 --> 00:34:21,290
but a full script too.

833
00:34:21,290 --> 00:34:23,230
We need to anticipate
every possible scenario

834
00:34:23,230 --> 00:34:24,550
and rehearse it all.

835
00:34:25,370 --> 00:34:26,370
It's so hard.

836
00:34:26,520 --> 00:34:27,330
It is hard.

837
00:34:28,320 --> 00:34:29,920
We have to nail it in one take.

838
00:34:30,070 --> 00:34:30,880
No NG.

839
00:34:31,650 --> 00:34:33,010
We have to pull this off.

840
00:34:33,040 --> 00:34:34,030
Failure isn't an option.

841
00:34:34,030 --> 00:34:34,590
Understood.

842
00:34:34,590 --> 00:34:35,650
Amazing! Awesome!

843
00:34:35,710 --> 00:34:38,170
I hereby declare the price-raising plan...

844
00:34:38,179 --> 00:34:39,010
action!

845
00:34:42,659 --> 00:34:45,460
What brings you here?

846
00:34:46,710 --> 00:34:47,510
